  "latest_report": {
    "at": "2026-10-20T21:19:14.126043751Z",
    "severity": "problem",
    "summary": "No new lost HTTP jobs since the 04:17Z reboot (lost flat at 37, all at reboots, cause unproven, #97); WS lost_commands flat for about 3h at 1.078M (#53)",
    "body": "Verdict: still a problem because 37 accepted HTTP jobs are lost and unexplained. The count has not moved since the 04:17Z reboot (about 17h). The WebSocket loss has stopped climbing for about 3h.\n\nUptime: run since 2026-10-12 23:24Z (189h). Kills since last report: one, 20:23:19Z (pid 1490 up about 54 min at 21:17Z). Kills since the 04:17Z reboot: 08:03, 12:35, 17:02, 20:23 (gaps 4h32m, 4h27m, 3h21m). Full reboot: 04:17:11Z Oct 20. Next due about 16:17Z Oct 21.\n\nLedger since 18:20Z report:\n- lost 37 -\u003e 37. Breakdown: 10 at the Oct 14 reboot, 24 at Oct 18 15:20Z, 3 at Oct 20 04:17Z.\n- lost_within_flush_window_of_kill 332 -\u003e 342 (+10). All accepted 20:23:19.54-.57Z before the 20:23:19.57Z kill. Expected bucket.\n- accepted 317.27M. failed_webhooks 107,697 -\u003e 109,721. finished_without_webhook 4,641. duplicate_webhooks 2,499, all within 10 min of restarts. late_webhooks_after_ledger_closed 0. stuck_over_24h 0.\n- WS lost_commands 1,036,522 (18:19Z) -\u003e 1,077,990 (21:17Z). Hourly rows: 1,077,695, 1,077,817, 1,077,858 for the last three hours, so +40 to +130 per hour, down from about 12-14k/h earlier. messages_after_expiry 4.84M. Lost vs late still unknown (#53).\n\nTrends (168 hourly rows, contiguous):\n- Median of hour-end values per day, Oct 14-18: RSS 269-276 MB, heap 188-197 MB, fds 853-866, goroutines 1,787-1,836, Pebble 912-929 MB. Bounded.\n- Oct 19: RSS 278, heap 207, fds 892, goroutines 1,882, accept p99 433 ms (Oct 16-18: 393 ms). Oct 20 partial: heap 210, fds 945, goroutines 2,025, accept p99 433 ms.\n- That is a mild upward drift over the last two days in goroutines, fds, heap and accept p99. Two days is not a leak trend. Watch Oct 21.\n- Goroutine peak 14,745 at the Oct 19 16:00 combined-peak hour. Other days' 16:00 peaks were 10.7k-11.9k.\n- HTTP ramp ceiling 750/s on Oct 13, 15, 17, 19. Not falling. The WS ramp stalled at the 200-session step again on Oct 20 (95.5/s, ceiling 0), as on Oct 14, 16 and 18.\n- WS daily lost_commands Oct 13-19: 179k, 117k, 123k, 98k, 43k, 74k, 204k. Not a steady decline; Oct 19 is the highest since Oct 13.\n\nHarness: hourly rows contiguous. minutes_target_unreachable only in kill and reboot hours. No generator_saturated in the last 180 minutes. Only driver gap still 01:18Z Oct 17 (about 3 min, 0 webhooks in it), cause unknown.\n\nUnexplained:\n1. 37 HTTP jobs lost at full reboots (#97). A 04:39Z comment on #97 proposes a driver accounting artifact: the driver excuses only jobs accepted up to 50 ms after the reboot request, but the supervisor kills about 200 ms later. The fix is merged as #93 but not deployed to this driver. The timing (165-190 ms) fits, but I cannot verify it from the status pages. If it holds, the 37 are a driver artifact and the counter is not trustworthy until #93 is deployed.\n2. WS lost_commands 1.08M (#53): lost or late unknown.\n3. Mild drift on Oct 19-20 (above).\n4. Oct 16 20:34Z EMFILE exit is still not in /events.\n5. WS ramp stall at 200 sessions.\n\nRuled out: new HTTP loss since 04:17Z; loss outside the flush window at the 4 kills since 04:17Z; memory and Pebble growth across days; harness outage.\n\nNext: check whether the 16:17Z Oct 21 reboot keeps HTTP lost at 37. Confirm whether #93 is deployed to the driver before that reboot, since that decides whether the 37 are real. Check whether the Oct 19-20 drift persists in Oct 21 steady hours. Trace WS command IDs (#53)."
  },
